Original commit body from 9de80e67a05395196de124761524cbb5dfe0b781:

CI caught the previous commit hand-editing SECURITY.md, which is GENERATED
between sentinel markers by scripts/generate-security-md. All four of my edits
sat inside the generated block and would have been silently wiped on the next
regeneration -- the same defect class the commit was fixing, one level up.

The corrections now live in the generator, and the measured verdicts are read
from docs/hypergumbo.claims.expected.json -- the SAME snapshot
scripts/check-self-claims diffs the live run against. So the prose and the gate
cannot disagree by construction: changing one without the other fails CI.

Each claim is rendered with the verdict actually measured for it, and the
section opens with the count table (2 violated / 16 inconclusive / 0 confirmed)
rather than presenting all eighteen as assurances.

Also corrected in the generator, not the artifact: the Known Limitations
paragraph asserted 'the load-bearing claims verify cleanly'. They do not -- they
are inconclusive. It now states that, plus the two limits that bound every
confirmed verdict this tool emits anywhere: pathlib.Path method calls are
invisible to the I/O catalogue, and one call edge is enough to pass the coverage
check while the rest of a language's call structure stays unanalysable.

Determinism contract re-verified: generate twice, --check clean.

